      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have one issue with everything you've just said. That extra step should already be in the form of 2FA. If the security was working correctly you would need a 2FA code to just login to your account. So just knowing the email and password should not be enough for gaining access to change those details.\nJust to be clear I'm not opposed to your request as confirming login to make profile/security changes is widely used for sure and a welcome addition. Also a confirmation email that allows the user to reclaim their account if a change was made without their permission is a good security addition.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
