  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-03T16:57:57.695Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I had sent in a ticket about this issue, but my feature request is through the website. While it is easy for users to change their email through the website, it does seem to be pretty insecure, as you really only need the current email associated, your new email, and your password. Due to the increased hacked accounts, I believe there needs to be an extra step involved here. \nMy suggestion is, when changing your email on the site, you must submit your current email first to receive a link to the associated email on the account, and from that email, that link takes you to a separate page that you must confirm the new email AS WELL AS confirming your password and/or using your 2FA code if you have it set up. Also included in this email should be a link to reset your password if this was fraudulent. I believe this will cut down on A LOT of potentially hacked accounts. The only reason I bring this up is because someone hacked my friend's account last week and it would really suck if they put so much time and effort into the account just to lose it all to a hacker. \nThank you.",
